# 1. Build Web Scrapers for Different Websites

## Purpose

Web scraping extracts data from websites automatically.

## Install Libraries

```bash id="3m5spj"
pip install requests beautifulsoup4

## Example: Website Title Scraper

## File: `web_scraper.py`

```python id="y0y8z6"
import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

url = "https://example.com"

headers = {
    "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0"
}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers)

soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, "html.parser")

titles = soup.find_all("h1")

for title in titles:
    print(title.text)

## Features

✅ Extract website data
✅ Use User-Agent headers
✅ Parse HTML content

# 2. Create Automation Scripts for Repetitive Tasks

## Purpose

Automate repeated manual work.

## Example: File Organizer Automation

## File: `file_organizer.py`

```python id="xv73kk"
import os
import shutil

folder = "Downloads"

for file in os.listdir(folder):

    path = os.path.join(folder, file)

    if file.endswith(".pdf"):

        target = os.path.join(folder, "PDFs")

        os.makedirs(target, exist_ok=True)

        shutil.move(path, os.path.join(target, file))

        print(f"{file} moved")

## Features

✅ Automatic file sorting
✅ Folder creation
✅ Repetitive task automation

# 3. Develop GUI Applications with Tkinter

## Purpose

Create graphical applications for users.

## Example: Tkinter GUI

## File: `gui_app.py`

```python id="u8ijqn"
import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import messagebox

def hello():

    messagebox.showinfo(
        "Message",
        "Automation Suite Running"
    )

root = tk.Tk()

root.title("Automation App")

root.geometry("400x300")

btn = tk.Button(
    root,
    text="Run",
    command=hello,
    width=20
)

btn.pack(pady=50)

root.mainloop()

## Features

✅ Buttons
✅ Windows
✅ User interaction
✅ Alerts and messages

